From: ThaRae <76752281+ThaRae@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:51:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibWebView+WebContent+Hub+UI/Qt: Run menu Copy and Cut
 through the page

The context menu's Copy read the selection out of the page from the UI
process, and Cut did the same through the Hub, so neither fired the DOM
copy and cut events. Pages that implement editing themselves, such as
contenteditable editors, therefore did nothing, while the keyboard
shortcuts worked because WebContent runs the clipboard actions for
those.

Run the copy and cut actions in WebContent for both the context menu
and the application menu, as the keyboard shortcuts do, and give the
page user activation first so that it may write the clipboard. The UI
asks the Hub for them with view_copy_selection and view_cut_selection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
